[38;5;246m⏺ [39mUser answered Claude's questions:
[38;5;246m  ⎿  · The repo has no test or lint tooling. What should this change set up? → Node test runner only (Recommended)[39m

[38;5;231m⏺[39m One consequence of choosing [38;5;153mnode --test[39m: the module has to be loadable outside a browser. So [38;5;153msettings.js[39m gets a small
  tail —

  [34mif[39m ([34mtypeof[39m module !== [31m"undefined"[39m && module.exports) {
    module.exports = { resolveEnvironment, buildSettings, ENVIRONMENTS };
  }

  — which the browser ignores and Node uses. The [38;5;153mwindow.AppSettings[39m assignment is guarded by [38;5;153mtypeof window !== [39m
  [38;5;153m"undefined"[39m, so importing the file under Node doesn't try to read [38;5;153mlocation.hostname[39m. That also matches the CommonJS
  convention already in [38;5;153msrc/utils.js[39m.

  Tests go in [38;5;153mtest/settings.test.js[39m covering: each mapped hostname resolves to its environment, an unmapped hostname
  falls back to development, the fallback emits a warning, and [38;5;153mendpoints.login[39m composes base + path correctly.
  [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m gets [38;5;153m"scripts": { "test": "node --test" }[39m — still zero dependencies.

  [1mFull scope:[0m new [38;5;153msettings.js[39m, new [38;5;153mtest/settings.test.js[39m, edits to [38;5;153mapp.js[39m (drop the constant, read from settings) and
  [38;5;153mindex.html[39m (one script tag), and a [38;5;153mtest[39m script in [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m.

  Does this design look right? If so, I'll write it up as a spec at
  [38;5;153mdocs/hyperpowers/specs/2026-09-16-settings-module-design.md[39m (uncommitted), run it through the review gates, and hand
